ANX7625 Type-C support for the imola 6.18.32 kernel, so the UNO Q's USB-C port is dual role.

Backported from the Type-C support in the IQ-9075 kernel tree (kernel/qcom/lemans, 6.18.56), which carries
upstream's ANX7625 Type-C work: the driver registers a typec port for its "connector" child and drives the
usb-role-switch on the other end of the connector's graph (dwc3) from the data role the ANX7625's PD firmware
reports (DATA_ROLE_STATUS in SYSTEM_STSTUS). Left out: that tree's unrelated drm_atomic_state ->
drm_atomic_commit rename in the bridge enable/disable hooks. Needs dr_mode = "otg" (usb-adb-debug.sh), or
probe defers forever waiting for a role switch dwc3 never registers. Applied by anx7625-typec.sh.

